{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And he burned in fire.</b> There is a substance that one puts in fire together with the gold, and as soon as the gold is burned it becomes black forever and will never again become gold." "<b>And he made the children of Israel drink.</b> According to the plain sense, he did not intend to make them drink, but rather to scatter the gold of the calf and eliminate it from the world. But when they drank from the water in which it was scattered, it appeared as though they had drunk it. And a proof for this matter: for it is written in the section of Ekev, ״ואכות אותו טחון״ (and I will grind it), and it is not written ״and I will make the children of Israel drink.״"], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:01:31.026878471Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}